i/code_combo/7b5033c1/28/code.py:20:#    The two changes interact: the color cycle determines both which endpoint is correct and how\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dfadab01/_logs/17.log:1739:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7b5033c1/28/code.py:24:#    count, with at least 4 folded rows. This keeps the repeated cycle obvious and gives several\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dfadab01/_logs/17.log:1740:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7b5033c1/28/code.py:31:#      repeating palette cycle, with a top-left fallback only for malformed inputs.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dfadab01/_logs/17.log:1741:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7b5033c1/28/code.py:39:#    Across examples, the input snake visibly cycles through a small repeated palette, and the\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dfadab01/_logs/17.log:1742:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7b5033c1/28/code.py:41:#    same cycle length. A human can infer the direction by following the repeating color rhythm,\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dfadab01/_logs/17.log:1743:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7b5033c1/28/code.py:48:#    The palette is capped at 3-5 colors and the stream is an exact ascending cycle, not an\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dfadab01/_logs/17.log:1744:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7b5033c1/28/code.py:54:#      palette cycle. Guaranteed by assigning cycle colors from the non-top-left endpoint.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dfadab01/_logs/17.log:1745:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7b5033c1/28/code.py:103:def _cycle_mismatch_count(colors: list[int], palette: list[int]) -> int:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dfadab01/_logs/17.log:1746:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7b5033c1/28/code.py:149:    mismatch_scores = [_cycle_mismatch_count(colors, palette) for colors in traced_colors]\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dfadab01/_logs/17.log:1747:/home/lixinyu/snap/n