:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/221dfab4/16/code.py:63:#      stripe cycle and the stop behavior are visible.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dfadab01/_logs/17.log:5968:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/221dfab4/16/code.py:208:    cycle = [int(Y), int(Y), int(G)]\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dfadab01/_logs/17.log:5969:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/221dfab4/16/code.py:221:        col = int(cycle[int(step) % 3])\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dfadab01/_logs/17.log:5970:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/16de56c4/10/code.py:21:#    replaces the single paint color with a visible color cycle read from the line's\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dfadab01/_logs/17.log:5971:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/16de56c4/10/code.py:26:#    - the color cycle is built once from all non-bg dots on that line, in visible\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dfadab01/_logs/17.log:5972:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/16de56c4/10/code.py:28:#    - each ray consumes that shared cycle starting from its own first marker's\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dfadab01/_logs/17.log:5973:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/16de56c4/10/code.py:29:#      position in the cycle, then later-starting rays overwrite earlier paint\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dfadab01/_logs/17.log:5974:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/16de56c4/10/code.py:32:#      cycle = [A,A,B,B,C]\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dfadab01/_logs/17.log:5975:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/16de56c4/10/code.py:35:#             cycle -> paints B,B,C and overwrites A at 4 and 10\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dfadab01/_logs/17.log:5976:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/16de56c4/10/code.py:38:#    a shared visible cycle.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dfadab01/_logs/17.log:5977:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/16de56c4/10/code.py:45:#    at most one extra dot per line, so the cycle stays short and legible.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dfadab01/_logs/17.log:5978:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/16de56c4/10/code.py:51:#    - \\\"one scalar paint per line\\\" is false; each ray now walks a cycle.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dfadab01/_logs/17.log:5979:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/16de56c4/10/code.py:70:#    ordered from the edge outward, the shared cycle is visible directly from spatial\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dfadab01/_logs/17.log:5980:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/16de56c4/10/code.py:73:#    overwrite color comes from the shared cycle rather than from a fixed marker or\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dfadab01/_logs/17.log:5981:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/16de56c4/10/code.py:104:#      the generator enforces it to keep the shared cycle visually easy to read.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dfadab01/_logs/17.log:5982:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/16de56c4/10/code.py:144:    Fill several periodic rays from one dominant edge, with each ray walking a shared visible color cycle.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dfadab01/_logs/17.log:5983:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/16de56c4/10/code.py:155:      ordered color list that will be reused as a cycle.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dfadab01/_logs/17.log:5984:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/16de56c4/10/code.py:166:      line as a repeating cycle, and start that cycle at the ray's own first marker.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dfadab01/_logs/17.log:5985:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/16de56c4/10/code.py:173:    rays, and where each ray enters the common visible cycle.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dfadab01/_logs/17.log:5986:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/16de56c4/10/code.py:212:        cycle = [color for _, color in ordered_dots]\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dfadab01/_logs/17.log:5987:/h